Package: tcspecial-moc
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: David VomLehn <dvomlehn@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: @SHLIBS@, python3
Recommends: python3-yaml, python3-tk, pkgconf
Replaces: tcspecial-ground
Conflicts: tcspecial-ground
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/vomlehn/tcspecial
Description: tcspecial's ground libraries and configuration editor
 What a ground station for tcspecial is built on: libtcsmoc-c, the TCSpecial
 MOC Correspondent (tcsmoc) for C and C++, with its header tcsmoc-c.h
 and pkg-config file tcsmoc-c.pc; the Python packages tcsprotocol (TCS
 Link Support), tcsmoc (the Correspondent) and tcs_ui; and tcs-gui, the
 graphical configuration editor, with its node descriptions and schemas.
 Everything is under /opt/tcs. /etc/ld.so.conf.d/tcspecial-moc.conf puts
 /opt/tcs/lib on the loader's path, a .pth file puts the Python packages on
 python3's, and /etc/profile.d/tcspecial-moc.sh puts /opt/tcs/bin and
 /opt/tcs/lib/pkgconfig on the shell's and pkg-config's.
